{
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "annotation": "This workflow performs metagenome assembly and multi-tool binning of paired short reads and optional long reads to generate dereplicated Metagenome-Assembled Genomes (MAGs), and analyzes them for quality and abundance.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "id": 0,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                100,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 1. Inputs and controls\n\nOriginal reads, optional long reads and metadata.\n\nGrouping: original / grouped / hybrid.\nCoverage: single / multi / both.\nRefiner: DAS Tool / Binette / both."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 1,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                1300,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 2. Read grouping\n\nThree independent subworkflows preserve library type.\n\nHybrid uses grouped-first union. Group names must not contain underscores."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 2,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                4300,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 3. Assembly\n\nAssembly is a real subworkflow: MEGAHIT, metaSPAdes or custom assemblies.\n\nCustom assembly identifiers and order must match the selected read collection."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 3,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                4900,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 4. Coverage strategies\n\n**Single-coverage binning (own/merged reads)** maps selected reads to their assembly.\n\n**Multi-coverage binning (all samples)** always uses original per-sample reads."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 4,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                6700,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 5. Refinement and reconciliation\n\nEach coverage branch reconciles DAS Tool and Binette outputs in the parent.\n\nFlatten → merge → re-nest avoids skipped nested-collection asymmetry. Conflicts across coverage branches get suffixes."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 5,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                8700,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 6. MAG quality and filtering\n\nOriginal CheckM2 quality assessment and dRep filtering/dereplication are retained."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 6,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                9950,
                -40
            ],
            "size": [
                440,
                280
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 7. Abundance and reports\n\nCoverM abundance, CheckM/CheckM2/QUAST assessment and MultiQC reporting are retained.\n\nMember-restricted co-assembly coverage is an unimplemented alternative, not the current multi strategy."
            }
        }
    ],
